{"page": 18, "text": "We made cash contributions to our international qualified defined benefit pension plans of $0.9 million and $0.6 million for the nine months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025, respectively. 16 Table of Contents NOTE 12. INCOME TAXES The Company\u2019s effective tax rate fluctuates from period to period based on several factors, including the geographic mix of earnings, the level of income or loss relative to available tax attributes, the recognition of valuation allowances in certain jurisdictions, and discrete tax items. For the three months ended September 30, 2026, the Company recorded income before taxes of $17.1 million and an associated income tax provision of $2.7 million, resulting in an effective tax rate of 15.8%. The income tax provision for the three months ended September 30, 2026 was primarily attributable to the tax on income before taxes for the period and an expense from valuation allowances on state credits, partially offset by the impact from a higher estimated annual effective tax rate compared with the prior quarter. For the three months ended September 30, 2025, the Company recorded income before taxes of $41.5 million and an associated income tax benefit of $(2.2) million, resulting in a negative effective tax rate of (5.3)%. The income tax benefit for the three months ended September 30, 2025 was primarily attributable to Inflation Reduction Act (IRA) production tax credits, partially offset by a change in tax contingencies and tax on income before taxes for the period. For the nine months ended September 30, 2026, the Company recorded the loss before taxes of $(97.4) million and an associated income tax benefit of $(15.5) million, resulting in an effective tax rate of 15.9%. The income tax benefit for the nine months ended September 30, 2026 was primarily attributable to tax on the loss before taxes for the period and IRA production tax credits recognized during the period, partially offset by an expense from prior year tax positions and an expense from valuation allowances on state credits. For the nine months ended September 30, 2025, the Company recorded income before taxes of $36.8 million and an associated income tax benefit of $(5.3) million, resulting in a negative effective tax rate of (14.4)%. The income tax benefit for the nine months ended September 30, 2025 was primarily attributable to IRA production tax credits recognized during the period, partially offset by a change in tax contingencies and tax on income before taxes for the period. As of September 30, 2026, we had $23.7 million of gross unrecognized tax benefits, which would have impacted the effective tax rate, if recognized. The changes in amounts of unrecognized tax benefits were as follows:\nNine Months Ended September 30,\n2026 2025\nUnrecognized Tax Benefits ($ in millions)\nBalance at beginning of year $ 24.0 $ 21.1\nIncreases for prior year tax positions 0.9 11.7\nDecreases for prior year tax positions (0.7) (0.5)\n"}
